foundation.question_text:
Name the solid made by this net.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\foreach \x/\y in {0/1,1/1,2/1,3/1,1/0,1/2}{\draw (\x,\y) rectangle ++(1,1);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Name the solid made by this net.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (1.2,2); \draw (1.2,0) rectangle (2.4,2); \draw (2.4,0) rectangle (3.6,2);
\draw (1.2,2)--(1.8,3.1)--(2.4,2)--cycle; \draw (1.2,0)--(1.8,-1.1)--(2.4,0)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Name the solid made by this net.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (2,2); \draw (0,0)--(1,-1.5)--(2,0)--cycle; \draw (2,0)--(3.5,1)--(2,2)--cycle; \draw (2,2)--(1,3.5)--(0,2)--cycle; \draw (0,2)--(-1.5,1)--(0,0)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does this net fold to a cube? Explain.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\foreach \x/\y in {0/0,1/0,2/0,0/1,1/1,2/1}{\draw (\x,\y) rectangle ++(1,1);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
Identify the solid and name its base shape.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (1,1) rectangle (3,2); \draw (1,0) rectangle (3,1); \draw (1,2) rectangle (3,3); \draw (1,3) rectangle (3,4); \draw (0,1) rectangle (1,2); \draw (3,1) rectangle (4,2);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

One triangle is missing from this pattern. What solid could it become after the missing face is added?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (1.2,2); \draw (1.2,0) rectangle (2.4,2); \draw (2.4,0) rectangle (3.6,2);
\draw (1.2,2)--(1.8,3.1)--(2.4,2)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Explain why the outer triangles meet at one point when this net folds.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (2,2); \draw (0,0)--(1,-1.5)--(2,0)--cycle; \draw (2,0)--(3.5,1)--(2,2)--cycle; \draw (2,2)--(1,3.5)--(0,2)--cycle; \draw (0,2)--(-1.5,1)--(0,0)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The pattern has four triangles but no base polygon. What must be added to make a square-pyramid net?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(1.2,-1.5)--(2.4,0)--cycle; \draw (2.4,0)--(3.6,1.5)--(2.4,3)--cycle; \draw (2.4,3)--(1.2,4.5)--(0,3)--cycle; \draw (0,3)--(-1.2,1.5)--(0,0)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
